# Quicksave — /bughunt full-codebase pass on GridGameGaiden: search done, fix phase complete, report delivered
_Printed: 2026-10-12_

## Current task
`/bughunt` (no time argument → exhaustive single pass, then unlimited fix phase) was run against
the whole GridGameGaiden repo. **Both phases are done and the final report has already been given
to the user in this session.** There is no pending work unless the user asks a follow-up (e.g.
"now commit this" or "go fix the architecture issue you flagged as needs-human-input"). If resuming
cold, the most likely next ask is one of those two, or reviewing the diff before committing.

## Decisions locked this session
- No time budget given → did one exhaustive pass across all tracked source, not a clock-bounded one.
- Used 6 parallel fresh `general-purpose` subagents (not forks) to read-only-review disjoint module
  sets in parallel, each reporting file:line findings back; then fixed everything myself directly
  (Read/Edit) in the main thread rather than delegating fixes.
- Did **not** commit or push anything — bughunt instructions say leave fixes in the working tree for
  the user to review. All fixes are uncommitted in the working tree alongside the large pre-existing
  uncommitted diff that was already there before this session started (see `git status` — ~40+ files
  were already modified/untracked before I touched anything).
- Dropped two "findings" as false positives after verifying against `docs/BIBLE.md`:
  - `Camp.Use`'s whole-party heal bypassing the expedition inn-lock — bible line 1626 explicitly says
    "the inn is closed on the road; **Tents still work**." Intentional, not a bug.
  - Several Core/Rules agent findings (EnemyPlanner footprint-step shove behavior, PincerDetector,
    TargetResolver, Formulas combat math) — all matched documented/bible behavior on inspection.
- Left exactly one thing unfixed as a genuine architecture decision (see Open questions below)
  rather than risk changing the battle engine's command/event contract without owner sign-off.
- Verification gate used throughout: `dotnet test Tests/Core.Tests/Core.Tests.csproj` (287 tests)
  plus, at the very end, the full `tools/test.ps1 -Compile` (Unity batchmode compile + all 287 tests
  + glyph check + asset check) since Unity Editor was NOT running at the time (checked via `tasklist`).
  Everything is green: 287/287 passed, 0 `error CS`, glyph check OK (37 files), asset check OK.

## State / where we are
Search phase (6 parallel subagents, each briefed with the relevant bible Laws) covered:
1. Core/Battle (BattleEngine, BattleRunner*, BattleState, Commands, ManaBank, Timeline, Unit,
   BattleConfig, BattleEvents, BattleRecorder)
2. Core/Rules + Core/Bot + Core/Content (EnemyPlanner, Formulas, PincerDetector, TargetResolver,
   Coord, Rng, HeroBot, MetaBot, ContentDb, ContentLoader, ContentModels)
3. Meta (CampRoutine, MetaServices, SaveData)
4. App/Battle (BattleScreen*.cs, BoardView, GameApp)
5. App/Screens + Services + UI + Automation (HubScreens, MenuScreens, PostBattleScreen, Art, Audio,
   Fonts, SaveStore, ScreenRouter, Tween, Ui, AutomationServer, StartScreens)
6. Python tooling (androidcheck, artreview, check_assets, check_glyphs, eyesheet, eyezoom, harness,
   import_art, make_icons, make_pixel_icons, make_sfx, make_tiles, records, uicheck)

Fix phase: ~24 candidate findings reviewed; the vast majority were real and got fixed. Full
bug→fix→verification table was already delivered to the user in the previous message — not
repeated here in full, but every fixed file is listed under Anchors below with what changed.

One standout bug worth remembering if asked about this session: a **live, currently-shipping
tofu-box bug** was found and fixed — under the "Roboto" or "Play" body-font presets (added
2026-10-11), the combat feed's `→` (U+2192) glyph was covered by neither that font nor
NotoSans/NotoSansSymbols2, so it would render as a missing-glyph box. Root-caused to `Fonts.cs`
only giving the "Classic"(Outfit) preset an implicit Outfit fallback; fixed by making every preset
fall back through Outfit as a final step, and updated `tools/check_glyphs.py`'s coverage set to
match (was previously checking Outfit+NotoSans+NotoSansSymbols2 as a flat union, which accidentally
masked the regression — now correctly mirrors the real runtime fallback chain). Verified concretely
with a one-off fontTools script showing U+2192 missing from Roboto/Play/NotoSans/NotoSansSymbols2
but present in Outfit/Lato/Montserrat/Inter.

Another standout: `SwapWeapon` in `BattleRunner.Abilities.cs` always reset an incoming bar-weapon to
its **factory** durability, meaning repeatedly swapping a weapon to the bar and back was a free,
unlimited "repair" exploit defeating the whole weapon-durability/shatter economy. Fixed by adding
`AbilitySlot.WeaponDurability` so swaps now preserve each weapon's actual wear.

## Open questions / pending
- **`BattleScreen.cs:1043`** (`Retreat()`) sets `State.Phase = BattlePhase.Retreated` directly,
  bypassing `BattleEngine.Apply` entirely — the one confirmed violation of GG-LAW-9 ("presentation
  never mutates state"). Correct fix = add a `RetreatCommand` through the Core command/event
  contract, which changes `BattleRecorder`/replay semantics — judged too architecturally
  significant to auto-fix under a bughunt pass. **Left as needs-human-input.** Immediate practical
  risk (abandoned coroutines bleeding into the next screen) was mitigated by making `Retreat()`
  no-op while `playing` is true (same `Busy` gating convention as `CanCommand()`), but the law
  violation itself is still there if the user wants it properly fixed.
- Related, lower-priority: `BattleScreen`'s many `App.StartCoroutine`-owned animations (CutIns.cs,
  Fx.cs, Playback.cs) aren't tracked/cancelled as a group on screen teardown — only the Retreat path
  was closed off. A full fix means a broader coroutine-ownership refactor; left as a design decision.
- `AutomationServer.cs`'s dev-only `DevGiveMana`/`DevSetBar`/`DevHp`/`DevBuff`/`DevQueueCast` mutate
  `BattleState` directly (also a law violation) — but these are explicitly-labeled dev cheats gated
  behind `DEVELOPMENT_BUILD`, judged accepted debt, not fixed.
- Nothing has been committed. If the user wants this committed, need to decide whether to bundle it
  with the large pre-existing uncommitted diff or split it into its own commit — not yet discussed.

## Next concrete steps
1. If the user says "commit this" — run `git status`/`git diff` first to separate the bughunt fixes
   from the pre-existing uncommitted work if they want them split; otherwise just commit per
   instructions (never `git add -A`; add specific files).
2. If the user says "fix the Retreat architecture issue" — design a `RetreatCommand` through
   `Core/Battle/Commands.cs` → `BattleEngine.Apply` dispatch → `BattleRunner.cs`, emit a
   `BattleEvent` for it, then update `BattleScreen.Retreat()` to call `Commit(new RetreatCommand())`
   instead of mutating `State.Phase` directly. Re-run `tools/test.ps1 -Compile` after.
3. Otherwise, nothing pending — the bughunt is complete and was already reported to the user in
   full in this conversation.

